<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Sept 27.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Sept 27.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Thursday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Portman Min	    293.65   1.85</p>
<p> 2   Niugini Min	    272.66   3.79</p>
<p> 3   Mayne Nickless	 191.63   8.47</p>
<p> 4   Adel Bton Cement     123.19   1.70</p>
<p> 5   Colonial Coml	  117.49   2.15</p>
<p> 6   T N T		    112.23   1.56</p>
<p> 7   Herald Rsc	     100.88   1.14</p>
<p> 8   Forrestania Gold	81.35   2.05</p>
<p> 9   Cape Range		74.32   0.28</p>
<p>10   Westral Forest	  74.28   2.05</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Dominion Min	     3.02   0.73</p>
<p> 2   Computer Power	   3.20   3.28</p>
<p> 3   Premier Inv		3.44   0.61</p>
<p> 4   Parbury Ltd		5.37   0.63</p>
<p> 5   BTR Plc		    6.23   5.80</p>
<p> 6   McIntosh Sec	     6.27   0.78</p>
